{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact O3 head d33186062e5c5189ca55ad6fee536fa1960cd115 on builder/oauth-authorization-20261102, tree ddb9e7ab, for request 6909704e under promise bfe65c9e and review request b96cba4e. This approval covers the authorization server, the consent page, the grant control, codes, tokens, refresh, revocation and the connection list. It claims no deployment, no live host and no G3 continuation. One finding below must be settled before O4 opens registration on a Worker.\n\nScope. Main 9c1556fa is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head changes 56 paths, and the commit-message check passes for all 14 commits. No card path changes. Card run 41596818010 and Page run 41596824812 succeeded at 9bcb91f9. The record commit after that changes only docs/mcp.md, the note and nine manifests.\n\nThe gate exception meets the isolated test-file rule in docs/testing.md:\n\n- Gate 4 at 07af767b failed only in packages/cli/test/browser-boundary.test.ts. Every stage before plain passed, plain passed 3593 cases, and Native never ran.\n- 9bcb91f9 changes only that file, and no file imports it. The repair adds issueOwnAgentInvitation to the closed list and renames the title. packages/cli/src/browser.ts already exports that function. The equality check and the identity loop stay, so any other new export still fails the test.\n- Ledger runs 109 and 110 pass the owning compiler and the whole file with the repaired bytes.\n- The follow-up runs the stage that gate 4 never reached. native.exit and followup.exit both read exit 0, 1060 cases pass and two skip. source-before and source-after both record 9bcb91f9, tree 23151c38 and a clean status.\n- All four failed gates stay failures on the record.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Consent signs a grant control with the room's existing nonextractable key. The Worker resolves the client, never the browser. oauthGrant requires the body's client, redirect, challenge, resource and state digest to match. A redirect must pass both the redirect policy and the client's registered list.\n- #grantAuthority rereads the signer, the agent and the controller from Native at each grant. An admin passes. Anyone else must be the agent's controller and must hold every action the agent holds.\n- The issuer stores only digests of codes and tokens. A code lives 60 seconds and works once, and a replay inside that window ends the grant. Refresh rotates, and any reuse of a rotated refresh token ends the grant. Exchange and refresh reread standing and the row after every await.\n- Unavailable standing now answers 503 with Retry-After and charges no failure. That settles O1 item 1. Opening a transport no longer evicts a live grant, and the issuer ends the oldest grant when a ninth one opens. That settles O1 item 2.\n- Consent asks for a one-hour own-agent invitation, and ownAgentIssueInput refuses 24 hours or more. The scenario enrolls at one hour through the Membership 13 window. That settles O2 item 1. A new consent for the same controller and client reuses the enrolled agent, so a lost connector needs no new key. That settles O2 item 2.\n- The metadata fetch follows ruling 4fd73a3f. It admits only listed HTTPS origins and sends no credentials. It follows no redirect, and it stops at five seconds or 5 KiB.\n\nBrowser evidence. The 42a76281 unit records the ordinary Membership 13 flow and the Membership 8 controller flow. Each shows Allow, matching state and issuer, a wrong verifier refused before the right one, MCP initialize, browser Revoke and an immediate 401. Each room records one agent add and one enrollment, and the consent storage holds no code or token. The eb43ac23 unit records the invitation display and the admin reuse with no second enrollment. After eb43ac23, the source changes only helper imports, one class-field form and one type declaration, and Page CI passed at 9bcb91f9.\n\nEvidence. The ten O3 manifests hold 242 files. The focused and isolated manifests hash to 0d9fc182… and 3781c349…, as the request states. Every file matches its size and digest and is read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 12 digests in the note's table name manifest files. All 311 private files match their indexes. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Native membership still decides every grant, and the agent object owns its grants, codes and tokens. The Worker supplies the client and the policy.\n\nSecurity: no finding blocks this landing. One finding blocks O4:\n\n1. Anyone can fill client registration for good. POST /oauth/register needs no credential and writes to the single registry oauth-public-clients-1. That registry holds at most 1,000 clients and never removes one; the test \"refuses client 1001 without replacing a prior client\" pins that behavior. So 1,000 anonymous requests end dynamic registration on that Worker. The answer is 503 with Retry-After, but no retry ever succeeds, and no route or setting clears the table. Claude and ChatGPT use metadata documents and keep working. Goose and any other client that registers do not. Before O4 opens a Worker, make a full registry recoverable: for example, expire a registration that no grant uses, or replace the oldest unused one. Add a control in which client 1,001 succeeds after an unused registration expires.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One item for O4: a refresh retry ends the grant. If a host loses the refresh answer and sends the old refresh token again, the issuer sees a reused token and ends the grant. OAuth 2.1 allows that for public clients. O4's live runs should record whether Claude or ChatGPT ever retries a refresh.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1c7d64e5117580e8b5d08f1db80cba8cf46f5d4b","binding":"assigned","head":"d33186062e5c5189ca55ad6fee536fa1960cd115","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b8d93534556195ea53898e7d4b275a7169abb41\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bfe65c9e8ce847461cbc83ce7c8a240d1dcb562e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b8d93534556195ea53898e7d4b275a7169abb41","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}